   "fen": "rnbq1bnr/pppp1kpp/4pp2/8/2BPP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR b KQ - 1 4",
   "line": [
    "Bc4"
   ],
   "spoken": "Bc4 is better than Bd3 here — it loads up the d5 break to blast the centre, and d5 is dangerous because Black's queen sits undefended on the long diagonal.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Aim the bishop at the break that opens lines onto an undefended enemy queen."
